Here is the complete implementation of the PDF to Text Converter API using the Lumen framework, following the provided OpenAPI schema and requirements.

### Step 1: Create the Lumen Project
Run the following command to create a new Lumen project:
```bash
composer create-project --prefer-dist laravel/lumen .
```

### Step 2: Modify the Required Files

#### 1. `bootstrap/app.php`
This file is responsible for bootstrapping the application. We need to register the necessary components and middleware.

<FILEPATH>
bootstrap/app.php
</FILEPATH>
<CODE>
<?php

require_once __DIR__.'/../vendor/autoload.php';

$app = new Laravel\Lumen\Application(
    $_SERVER['APP_BASE_PATH'] ?? dirname(__DIR__)
);

// Load the environment variables
$app->configure('app');

// Register the routes
$app->router->group(['namespace' => 'App\Http\Controllers'], function ($router) {
    require __DIR__.'/../routes/api.php';
});

return $app;
</CODE>

#### 2. `routes/api.php`
This file defines the API routes for the application.

<FILEPATH>
routes/api.php
</FILEPATH>
<CODE>
<?php

use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Route;
use App\Http\Controllers\PDFController;

Route::post('/convert', [PDFController::class, 'convert']);
</CODE>

#### 3. `app/Http/Controllers/PDFController.php`
This controller handles the PDF to text conversion logic.

<FILEPATH>
app/Http/Controllers/PDFController.php
</FILEPATH>
<CODE>
<?php

namespace App\Http\Controllers;

use Illuminate\Http\Request;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Storage;

class PDFController extends Controller
{
    public function convert(Request $request)
    {
        // Validate the request
        $request->validate([
            'file' => 'required|file|mimes:pdf|max:2048',
        ]);

        // Store the uploaded PDF file temporarily
        $path = $request->file('file')->store('pdfs');

        // Convert PDF to text using pdftotext
        $text = $this->pdfToText(storage_path('app/' . $path));

        // Delete the temporary PDF file
        Storage::delete($path);

        // Return the extracted text
        return response($text, 200)->header('Content-Type', 'text/plain');
    }

    private function pdfToText($pdfPath)
    {
        // Use the pdftotext command to extract text from the PDF
        $output = [];
        $returnVar = 0;
        exec("pdftotext " . escapeshellarg($pdfPath) . " -", $output, $returnVar);

        if ($returnVar !== 0) {
            return response()->json(['error' => 'Conversion failed'], 500);
        }

        return implode("\n", $output);
    }
}
</CODE>

#### 4. `.env`
This file contains the environment configuration for the application.

<FILEPATH>
.env
</FILEPATH>
<CODE>
APP_NAME=Lumen
APP_ENV=local
APP_KEY=
APP_DEBUG=true
APP_URL=http://localhost

LOG_CHANNEL=stack

DB_CONNECTION=sqlite
DB_DATABASE=/app/db.sqlite3
</CODE>

### Step 3: Run the Application
To start the application, run the following command:
```bash
php -S 0.0.0.0:5000 -t public
```

### Summary
This implementation provides a simple API to convert PDF files to plain text. The API accepts a PDF file via a POST request to the `/convert` endpoint, processes it using the `pdftotext` utility, and returns the extracted text. The application is configured to use SQLite as the database, and it is set up to run on port 5000.
